 ## Background
-The technique is derived from Disney's Hyperion renderer, as described in "The Design and Evolution of Disney’s Hyperion Renderer" [S1, unofficial]. Hyperion is a production-quality renderer used for animated films. The method was implemented to address the computational cost of rendering dense clouds, which involve many scattering events over short distances in similar directions. The author of the source implemented the exponential decay strategy globally rather than the linear reduction between bounces 5 and 20 suggested in the paper, noting minimal visual difference while achieving faster performance due to fewer sampled events [S1, unofficial].
